.TH "WEBTRANSPORTSENDGROUP" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebTransportSendGroup \- WebTransportSendGroup
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]WebTransportSendGroup\f[B]\f[R] interface of the
WebTransport API represents a group of streams and datagrams, within
which relative send priority is determined by the \f[CR]sendOrder\f[R]
value of each member.
.PP
\f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] is a transferable object.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
.TP
\f[B]getStats()\f[R]
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with an object containing
statistics aggregated across all of the
\f[CR]WebTransportSendStream\f[R] and
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] objects currently associated
with this group.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unlike for \f[CR]WritableStream\f[R] instances, for which the priority
at which bytes are sent on different streams is
implementation\-dependent, a \f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] or
\f[CR]WebTransportSendStream\f[R] allows you to set the priority at
which bytes will be sent on each instance relative to others in the same
\f[CR]sendGroup\f[R].
A send group is created using the \f[CR]createSendGroup()\f[R] method,
and the relative priority is defined by the \f[CR]sendOrder\f[R]
property of \f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] or
\f[CR]WebTransportSendStream\f[R] instances.
Different groups are expected to be treated as equals for the purposes
of bandwidth allocation \(em though the precise way bandwidth is divided
between groups is implementation\-defined.
.PP
A \f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] is created using the
\f[CR]createSendGroup()\f[R] method of the \f[CR]WebTransport\f[R]
interface.
You can then associate it with a
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] or
\f[CR]WebTransportSendStream\f[R] by:
.IP \(bu 2
Passing it as the \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] option when the object is created
\(em see \f[CR]WebTransport.createUnidirectionalStream()\f[R],
\f[CR]WebTransport.createBidirectionalStream()\f[R], and
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.createWritable()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Setting the object\(cqs \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] property afterwards \(em
see \f[CR]WebTransportSendStream.sendGroup\f[R] and
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable.sendGroup\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The example below creates a send group, then associates a unidirectional
stream and the connection\(cqs outgoing datagram stream with it, giving
each a \f[CR]sendOrder\f[R].
Bytes on the datagram stream will be prioritized ahead of any bytes on
the unidirectional stream, because they are both in the same
\f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] and the datagram stream has a higher
\f[CR]sendOrder\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] sendGroup = transport.createSendGroup();

\f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]await\f[R] transport.createUnidirectionalStream({
  sendGroup,
  sendOrder: 1,
});

\f[B]const\f[R] datagrams = transport.datagrams.createWritable({
  sendGroup,
  sendOrder: 2,
});
.EE
